WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.476 --> 00:00:02.250
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:05.524
- [Kelly] Oh my God, I am
in love with your suit.

00:00:05.524 --> 00:00:06.452
That's my favorite color.

00:00:06.452 --> 00:00:07.809
- Yes, yes. Green's your favorite color?

00:00:07.809 --> 00:00:08.839
- [Kelly] Yes. Yes.

00:00:08.839 --> 00:00:09.724
- Oh, mine's red and blue.

00:00:09.724 --> 00:00:10.557
- [Kelly] It is?
- Yes.

00:00:10.557 --> 00:00:12.058
- It's very American of you.

00:00:12.058 --> 00:00:13.582
- Yes. Thank you.
- Red and blue.

00:00:13.582 --> 00:00:14.415
- Go USA.
- Yeah.

00:00:14.415 --> 00:00:17.535
I used to love you until you
said Cowboys were gonna win.

00:00:17.535 --> 00:00:19.654
And then look what happened.
I don't understand.

00:00:19.654 --> 00:00:21.242
Everybody was saying that we were gonna,

00:00:21.242 --> 00:00:22.649
look, we say it every year.

00:00:22.649 --> 00:00:24.238
I get it, but like,

00:00:24.238 --> 00:00:25.886
but I really did think, like,

00:00:25.886 --> 00:00:27.006
we had all the players.

00:00:27.006 --> 00:00:28.751
It was all there.

00:00:28.751 --> 00:00:30.811
- I know. I did that
pick for you, too, Kelly.

00:00:30.811 --> 00:00:32.070
- [Kelly] I, you, look-
- Yes.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:34.482
- Here's the thing. I yelled so hardcore.

00:00:34.482 --> 00:00:36.605
I became that crazy fan. Watch.

00:00:36.605 --> 00:00:39.428
I got really into football this season.

00:00:39.428 --> 00:00:40.725
I'm like into fantasy football.

00:00:40.725 --> 00:00:42.105
Do you, have you ever
played fantasy, as well?

00:00:42.105 --> 00:00:43.291
- I've never played fantasy football ever.

00:00:43.291 --> 00:00:44.124
- Really?

00:00:44.124 --> 00:00:46.021
- Mm mm. I know all
about fantasy football.

00:00:46.021 --> 00:00:46.854
- But you don't think about that?

00:00:46.854 --> 00:00:48.809
Like, as a football
player, you're like, man,

00:00:48.809 --> 00:00:50.978
what if these people were
all combined on one team?

00:00:50.978 --> 00:00:52.408
Well, you kind of had that 'cause, yeah.

00:00:52.408 --> 00:00:54.014
(audience laughs)

00:00:54.014 --> 00:00:55.353
- I actually knew how it worked.

00:00:55.353 --> 00:00:56.186
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:56.186 --> 00:00:57.800
- And like throughout the
season when I was playing,

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.496
I always made sure I was like, okay,

00:00:59.496 --> 00:01:01.115
if I can score a touchdown,

00:01:01.115 --> 00:01:02.565
there's like two minutes
left in the fourth quarter.

00:01:02.565 --> 00:01:04.535
We're already winning by
like three touchdowns.

00:01:04.535 --> 00:01:06.505
But if I can somehow sneak
another touchdown in-

00:01:06.505 --> 00:01:07.338
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:07.338 --> 00:01:09.087
- For my fantasy owners,
they're gonna love me.

00:01:09.087 --> 00:01:11.309
- That's what we say at home.

00:01:11.309 --> 00:01:13.060
Just walking in and then
you start getting angry

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:14.814
at the other players that you don't have.

00:01:14.814 --> 00:01:16.320
But it's so fun.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:19.917
Anyway, does it anger you
that fans, we use the word we?

00:01:19.917 --> 00:01:22.764
Like, we're like, we lost and,
like, we didn't do anything.

00:01:22.764 --> 00:01:24.183
Like does it, you know what I'm saying?

00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:26.128
- Actually, no. It
doesn't anger me at all.

00:01:26.128 --> 00:01:28.620
Because without the fans,
we wouldn't have the NFL.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:29.553
We wouldn't have the game.

00:01:29.553 --> 00:01:31.563
- [Kelly] Well, that's good. Good answer.

00:01:31.563 --> 00:01:32.995
- So, it's a collective.
- Good answer.

00:01:32.995 --> 00:01:34.342
- So, we makes sense.

00:01:34.342 --> 00:01:36.267
- Okay because I feel
insane at the end of that.

00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:38.116
My daughter's like, "Why
do you keep saying we?"

00:01:38.116 --> 00:01:39.813
And I'm like, "I used to be you. I know."

00:01:39.813 --> 00:01:41.035
But now I'm them.

00:01:41.035 --> 00:01:42.689
Anyway, what's like one of your favorite,

00:01:42.689 --> 00:01:44.922
'cause you have so many
great Super Bowl moments,

00:01:44.922 --> 00:01:46.186
like, what's one of your favorites?

00:01:46.186 --> 00:01:48.738
- My favorite Super Bowl
moment is when I won

00:01:48.738 --> 00:01:49.668
my first Super Bowl.

00:01:49.668 --> 00:01:51.031
I got into the Super Bowl Club.

00:01:51.031 --> 00:01:51.921
That's what it's all about.

00:01:51.921 --> 00:01:52.754
- [Kelly] So cool.

00:01:52.754 --> 00:01:53.727
- You just wanna get into that club.

00:01:53.727 --> 00:01:54.560
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.763
- And we beat the
Seattle Seahawks in 2015.

00:01:56.763 --> 00:01:57.962
They were going to be a,

00:01:57.962 --> 00:01:59.075
they were trying to be repeat champions-

00:01:59.075 --> 00:01:59.908
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:59.908 --> 00:02:01.414
- Which hasn't been
done in quite some time.

00:02:01.414 --> 00:02:02.305
It might be done this year

00:02:02.305 --> 00:02:04.611
for the first time since
the Patriots did it what?

00:02:04.611 --> 00:02:05.532
'03, '04?

00:02:05.532 --> 00:02:08.859
But that game that we
played was just spectacular.

00:02:08.859 --> 00:02:10.600
- Not Patriots, you mean Chiefs, right?

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:11.433
Or no, Patriot?
- Yeah.

00:02:11.433 --> 00:02:13.715
No, no, the Patriots were the
last one to go back to back.

00:02:13.715 --> 00:02:15.205
I think it was '03, '04.

00:02:15.205 --> 00:02:16.189
- [Kelly] Oh, I thought you
meant who's going this year.

00:02:16.189 --> 00:02:17.268
I was like, they're not going.

00:02:17.268 --> 00:02:18.966
- And if the Chiefs win this year again,

00:02:18.966 --> 00:02:21.728
they're the first team to go
back to back in Super Bowl wins

00:02:21.728 --> 00:02:23.837
since the Patriots, I think '03, '04.

00:02:23.837 --> 00:02:24.670
- Yeah.

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:25.503
- Right around those years.

00:02:25.503 --> 00:02:26.891
But that Super Bowl versus Seattle,

00:02:26.891 --> 00:02:29.003
Malcolm Butler with that game stealing-

00:02:29.003 --> 00:02:29.836
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:29.836 --> 00:02:30.669
- Interception to win the game.

00:02:30.669 --> 00:02:32.326
Let me tell you, it was
the most fabulous game

00:02:32.326 --> 00:02:34.877
of all time and one of the
best Super Bowls ever, too.

00:02:34.877 --> 00:02:36.508
- That's the thing about football.

00:02:36.508 --> 00:02:37.341
You never know.

00:02:37.341 --> 00:02:38.431
- [Rob] Yes.
- Yeah.

00:02:38.431 --> 00:02:40.440
- That's why there's a movie
called "Any Given Sunday."

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:41.491
- [Kelly] I love that soundtrack.

00:02:41.491 --> 00:02:42.324
- Yes.

00:02:42.324 --> 00:02:44.045
- Oh, Missy Elliott has
a good song on that.

00:02:44.045 --> 00:02:45.856
Of course, I went musical
with it. Whatever.

00:02:45.856 --> 00:02:49.345
So wait, so Super Bowl's in
Vegas. I'm gonna be there.

00:02:49.345 --> 00:02:50.343
You're gonna be there, obviously.

00:02:50.343 --> 00:02:53.757
So like, are you excited?
Are you a Vegas guy?

00:02:53.757 --> 00:02:55.026
- I'm a Vegas guy in a way.

00:02:55.026 --> 00:02:55.859
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:02:55.859 --> 00:02:57.526
- And I look at Vegas totally different

00:02:57.526 --> 00:02:58.671
than the way I looked at Vegas-

00:02:58.671 --> 00:02:59.504
- [Kelly] Amen.

00:02:59.504 --> 00:03:00.337
- When I was 22 years old-
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:00.337 --> 00:03:02.426
- 23 years old.
- You remember it now.

00:03:02.426 --> 00:03:04.624
- Yes, I didn't remember
it really back then.

00:03:04.624 --> 00:03:06.471
- Yeah.
- When I was that age.

00:03:06.471 --> 00:03:09.938
But Vegas I used to just think
was a complete party 24, 7.

00:03:09.938 --> 00:03:10.771
You have to go there-
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:10.771 --> 00:03:12.289
- You're drinking right
when you get off the plane.

00:03:12.289 --> 00:03:13.122
- You're drinking-

00:03:13.122 --> 00:03:14.180
- [Kelly] Oh, the most sick
I've ever been in my life.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:15.761
- Back on the plane when you're leaving

00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:17.022
and you're thinking all about

00:03:17.022 --> 00:03:19.082
what you just did the last 24 hours

00:03:19.082 --> 00:03:20.016
or 48 hours you were there.

00:03:20.016 --> 00:03:20.849
- Trying to recall it.

00:03:20.849 --> 00:03:21.891
- Yeah. Recall it.

00:03:21.891 --> 00:03:24.155
But I don't look at
Vegas like that anymore.

00:03:24.155 --> 00:03:25.797
You know, I'm a little bit more older.

00:03:25.797 --> 00:03:28.158
I like to go there now.
I like to go to shows.

00:03:28.158 --> 00:03:28.991
- Yeah.

00:03:28.991 --> 00:03:29.988
- I like to go to concerts.
- Yeah.

00:03:29.988 --> 00:03:31.770
I just like to enjoy the whole atmosphere

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:34.242
of what Vegas has to offer
and not just go there

00:03:34.242 --> 00:03:35.969
and just start raging right away.

00:03:35.969 --> 00:03:36.802
- Yeah.

00:03:37.674 --> 00:03:40.331
Those are for 20 year
olds that have the ability

00:03:40.331 --> 00:03:42.441
to wake up the next day
and not feel like death.

00:03:42.441 --> 00:03:43.964
- [Rob] Yes.
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah.

00:03:43.964 --> 00:03:45.283
- Yeah, those 20-year-old days.

00:03:45.283 --> 00:03:47.426
- Except I think we did
feel like death afterwards.

00:03:47.426 --> 00:03:49.153
We just kept going back.
It's like pregnancy.

00:03:49.153 --> 00:03:50.835
Why? Wait, why do we do it again?

00:03:50.835 --> 00:03:51.668
I don't know.

00:03:51.668 --> 00:03:53.324
I have to say it has to be
very different from, obviously,

00:03:53.324 --> 00:03:55.841
playing the actual game
to then being an analyst.

00:03:55.841 --> 00:03:57.873
Like, becoming that
and like talking about,

00:03:57.873 --> 00:03:59.560
like, was that hard?

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:02.310
- A little bit because, you know,

00:04:03.181 --> 00:04:05.296
I love to be put on the
spot, and fourth and goal,

00:04:05.296 --> 00:04:07.544
you know, on the five yard line,

00:04:07.544 --> 00:04:08.655
I'm used to that situation.

00:04:08.655 --> 00:04:10.611
I love that situation
when my number's called

00:04:10.611 --> 00:04:12.300
and I have to go up and make a play-

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:13.133
- Under pressure.

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:15.936
- But now I was using my body
and my mind in a physical way,

00:04:15.936 --> 00:04:17.819
and now I'm doing it
more in a mental way, so-

00:04:17.819 --> 00:04:18.652
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:18.652 --> 00:04:20.569
- So, we're on every
Sunday before the games.

00:04:20.569 --> 00:04:21.402
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:21.402 --> 00:04:22.823
- And now, it's like fourth and goal,

00:04:22.823 --> 00:04:23.947
but I'm doing it mentally.

00:04:23.947 --> 00:04:24.780
- Yeah.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:28.219
- And I gotta produce
live right on that spot

00:04:28.219 --> 00:04:29.660
right at the moment.
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:30.493
- Mentally, not physically anymore.

00:04:30.493 --> 00:04:32.542
So it's a little bit of a
different transformation.

00:04:32.542 --> 00:04:35.488
But I love it because I get
to offer my unique perspective

00:04:35.488 --> 00:04:36.765
to the game of football, as well.

00:04:36.765 --> 00:04:38.175
- [Kelly] We love it
as fans, watching you-

00:04:38.175 --> 00:04:39.037
- And it's just so much fun doing it.

00:04:39.037 --> 00:04:42.212
- Yeah. I said we again, whatever.

00:04:42.212 --> 00:04:44.535
That does work, we.

00:04:44.535 --> 00:04:47.701
Athletes do many of the same
things when they retire.

00:04:47.701 --> 00:04:50.109
Gronk and his former
teammate, Julian Edelman,

00:04:50.109 --> 00:04:52.191
recently had some fun with that.

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:53.664
So, let's see it.

00:04:53.664 --> 00:04:56.439
- We're retired athletes.
We're gonna get jobs on TV.

00:04:56.439 --> 00:04:58.546
- We're retired athletes.
We're gonna tease a comeback.

00:04:58.546 --> 00:04:59.523
- We're retired athletes.

00:04:59.523 --> 00:05:01.800
We're gonna watch our old highlights.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:04.607
- We're retired athletes.
We're gonna start a podcast.

00:05:04.607 --> 00:05:06.354
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:05:06.354 --> 00:05:08.646
- This should have been an
SNL skit. It's so funny.

00:05:08.646 --> 00:05:10.179
They should do that
with musicians, as well.

00:05:10.179 --> 00:05:11.170
- We're retired athletes.

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:12.664
We'll go on "The Kelly Clarkson Show."

00:05:12.664 --> 00:05:13.497
- There you go. Got it.

00:05:13.497 --> 00:05:15.397
Good times. Good times.

00:05:15.397 --> 00:05:18.643
So wait, whose idea was that?
Are you into social media?

00:05:18.643 --> 00:05:19.560
- [Rob] A little bit.

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:20.393
- Okay.

00:05:20.393 --> 00:05:21.538
- Yeah, social media's cool, you know.

00:05:21.538 --> 00:05:22.371
You gotta use it for the right reasons.

00:05:22.371 --> 00:05:23.204
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:23.204 --> 00:05:24.286
- But I was at Julian Edelman's house.

00:05:24.286 --> 00:05:26.408
He has a great podcast
called "Names with Games."

00:05:26.408 --> 00:05:27.241
- Yeah.

00:05:27.241 --> 00:05:28.239
- And we just did his podcast

00:05:28.239 --> 00:05:30.082
and he has his whole
social media team there.

00:05:30.082 --> 00:05:32.326
And then they showed me
this new trend on TikTok

00:05:32.326 --> 00:05:33.570
and that was the new trend.

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:35.365
And they were like, we're gonna
do it as retired athletes.

00:05:35.365 --> 00:05:36.789
And it was such a great idea.

00:05:36.789 --> 00:05:37.622
- [Kelly] So funny.

00:05:37.622 --> 00:05:38.455
- And it came out so good.

00:05:38.455 --> 00:05:39.698
- I know. I was telling you on the break.

00:05:39.698 --> 00:05:40.836
I was like, that should have been on SNL.

00:05:40.836 --> 00:05:43.169
That would've been a
really funny skit, yeah.

00:05:43.169 --> 00:05:46.154
So, you have a new partner for
big game parties. Who is it?

00:05:46.154 --> 00:05:47.258
- Yes, I actually do.

00:05:47.258 --> 00:05:49.654
And Julian Edelman is now
a part of it, as well.

00:05:49.654 --> 00:05:51.741
And this is my second year
teaming up with Bounty.

00:05:51.741 --> 00:05:53.002
And that's why I'm in my green suit

00:05:53.002 --> 00:05:55.329
because I am the Bounty man.

00:05:55.329 --> 00:05:56.612
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- Yes.

00:05:56.612 --> 00:05:57.866
- And green is a great color.

00:05:57.866 --> 00:06:00.007
- And I'm from Buffalo,

00:06:00.007 --> 00:06:02.517
so I know a thing or two
about Buffalo, you know,

00:06:02.517 --> 00:06:03.350
wings, as well.

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:04.183
- Yeah.

00:06:04.183 --> 00:06:05.016
- And you gotta always have blue cheese

00:06:05.016 --> 00:06:06.400
on the side when you're from Buffalo,

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:09.147
and you can't have football without wings,

00:06:09.147 --> 00:06:11.707
and you can't have wings without Bounty.

00:06:11.707 --> 00:06:13.227
- Okay. I can't have-

00:06:13.227 --> 00:06:14.353
- It gets saucy. It gets messy.

00:06:14.353 --> 00:06:16.892
The quicker pick upper
upper just comes and goes-

00:06:16.892 --> 00:06:17.725
- [Kelly] I got you.

00:06:17.725 --> 00:06:19.552
- Cleans you right up
- Quicker picker upper.

00:06:19.552 --> 00:06:20.385
I remember that.

00:06:20.385 --> 00:06:24.255
No, I agree with all of that,
except not the blue cheese.

00:06:24.255 --> 00:06:25.556
I have to have ranch.

00:06:25.556 --> 00:06:28.762
(audience cheers)

00:06:28.762 --> 00:06:30.485
- When you're from Buffalo-
- I'm Texan.

00:06:30.485 --> 00:06:33.378
- When you're from Buffalo,
you use blue cheese only.

00:06:33.378 --> 00:06:36.856
- When you're Texan, you put
ranch or ketchup on everything.

00:06:36.856 --> 00:06:38.635
- Yes, but when you're from Buffalo,

00:06:38.635 --> 00:06:39.839
you gotta have the Buffalo blue cheese.

00:06:39.839 --> 00:06:40.672
- Okay.

00:06:40.672 --> 00:06:41.690
- But if you're outside of Buffalo-

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:43.050
- Okay.
- I won't make the argument.

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:44.528
Yes, you can have ranch-

00:06:44.528 --> 00:06:45.361
- [Kelly] Just saying.

00:06:45.361 --> 00:06:46.194
- 'Cause the Buffalo blue cheese

00:06:46.194 --> 00:06:47.961
is the only legit blue cheese out there.

00:06:47.961 --> 00:06:49.046
- Yeah. I like blue cheese.

00:06:49.046 --> 00:06:51.765
I like blue cheese, but there's
something mm about ranch

00:06:51.765 --> 00:06:53.012
that I really love.

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:53.845
- Nope. Blue cheese.

00:06:53.845 --> 00:06:54.739
- Really, I just want the ranch.

00:06:54.739 --> 00:06:55.572
- You gotta go to Buffalo.

00:06:55.572 --> 00:06:56.578
- And I just wanna, I need something,

00:06:56.578 --> 00:06:58.276
the vessel for it to get-

00:06:58.276 --> 00:06:59.406
- Wait until you have
the Buffalo blue cheese.

00:06:59.406 --> 00:07:01.613
- Okay. I have had Buffalo blue.

00:07:01.613 --> 00:07:03.023
I like it. I like it.

00:07:03.023 --> 00:07:03.856
And maybe when I'm-

00:07:03.856 --> 00:07:05.039
- Where'd you go?
- In Buffalo, I'll do that.

00:07:05.039 --> 00:07:05.872
- Yes, when you're in Buffalo.

00:07:05.872 --> 00:07:06.995
- Everywhere else, I say no.

00:07:06.995 --> 00:07:09.567
So, if you weren't an athlete,

00:07:09.567 --> 00:07:10.550
and people ask me this about music,

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:11.407
but if you weren't an athlete,

00:07:11.407 --> 00:07:13.416
what do you think you'd be doing?

00:07:13.416 --> 00:07:14.249
- What would I be doing?

00:07:14.249 --> 00:07:15.765
Well, my dad, he's been
in the fitness industry

00:07:15.765 --> 00:07:18.733
for 33 years now, selling
fitness equipment.

00:07:18.733 --> 00:07:20.326
A couple of my brothers
sell the fitness equipment

00:07:20.326 --> 00:07:22.734
for him, as well, so I
love to workout still.

00:07:22.734 --> 00:07:24.072
- Does your whole family
look this athletic?

00:07:24.072 --> 00:07:24.988
You're just all? Okay.

00:07:24.988 --> 00:07:26.242
- Yes, they all do. Yes.

00:07:26.242 --> 00:07:27.131
- So does mine.

00:07:27.131 --> 00:07:28.353
- They stay fit, and actually,

00:07:28.353 --> 00:07:30.179
three of my brothers played in the NFL.

